-------------------------------------------------------
 Module 9: EDA/VLSI tool scripting (SDC-style)
-------------------------------------------------------

Sourcing constraints (SDC-style Tcl commands)
  (constraint) create_clock -name core_clk -period 900
  (constraint) set_max_delay 950 -from in2
Timing analysis
  in1    -> out1    arrival=  550ps  slack= 350.0ps  [MET]
  in2    -> out1    arrival=  720ps  slack= 180.0ps  [MET]
  in1    -> out2    arrival=  300ps  slack= 600.0ps  [MET]
  in2    -> out2    arrival= 1050ps  slack=-150.0ps  [VIOLATED]
  ---
  worst path: in2 -> out2, slack=-150.0ps
Sign-off decision (like a real flow's exit check)
TIMING NOT MET -- worst negative slack (WNS) = -150ps
-> would normally trigger another optimization/ECO pass
Why this matters
This is the exact shape of a PrimeTime/OpenSTA sign-off script:
  1. source design + constraints (Tcl procs standing in for real commands)
  2. walk timing paths and compute slack
  3. branch the flow based on the numeric result
Swap the toy arrays for a real netlist/SDC reader and the control
flow above is unchanged -- that's why Tcl has stayed the EDA
industry's scripting layer for decades.

